  "conclusions": [
    "Withdraw the v2 result as a universal sigma2/PPO recommendation. It selected a joint geometry/bin/range configuration, omitted sigma0.5 for that nonuniform family and screened out matched sigma comparisons before TD.",
    "Old TD policy utility exactly cancelled constant critic bias. New sampled clipped-PPO probes detect it; a regression test shows cancellation on-policy but not in clipped branches, and cancellation after advantage centering.",
    "At late mean3.8337/std0.3858, raw nonuniform\u00b150/K31/sigma2 has absolute sigma7.2103 (18.689x the target std). Sigma0.5 gives5.547x label-gradient contrast and15.440x label-location Fisher information. These are label properties, not proof that Adam or real PPO improves proportionally.",
    "Reducing raw-Gaussian sigma does not cure the nonuniform mean bias: sigma2 gives-0.024104; sigma0.75 gives-0.026598; sigma0.5 gives-0.027292. This reproduces the real logged-0.024101 bias without support overflow.",
    "For symlog-coordinate smoothing with raw expectation decode, sigma2 has+0.727790 projection bias versus+0.054199 at0.5 on the same\u00b150/K31 support and mean. Own-bootstrap training amplifies this; this is a concrete mechanism by which lower sigma can strongly help historical symlog implementations, not a claim identifying every past implementation.",
    "The correct constant-state lambda operator has bootstrap coefficient gamma*(1-lambda)/(1-gamma*lambda), not gamma. Raw nonuniform sigma2 predicts value bias-0.139125 and GAE bias+0.023382 in that model. Observed policy_loss-0.024813 is consistent with a positive GAE offset but is not direct evidence of mean GAE.",
    "In the matched late sphere/own-bootstrap cell, reducing raw nonuniform\u00b150 sigma2 to0.75 cuts PPO-gradient relative MSE9.28% while value NMSE becomes5.46% worse. Value-only selection can therefore miss consumer-usefulness differences.",
    "Sigma reduction alone is not robust for the cancelled geometry: on the offset-shift holdout its0.75 PPO-gradient error is worse than2. Tighter uniform-raw support with0.5/0.75 is the stronger next hypothesis, not a proven MuJoCo improvement."
  ],
